findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    reviewer flagged silent unknown-field acceptance but not the broader error-swallowing
    in from_file_or_default. No test checks that parse/permission errors propagate
    distinctly from NotFound.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: 'Security tests cover CWE-209: ''Error messages don''t leak credentials/tokens''.
    However, the reviewer did not flag the specific eprintln!("{e}") pattern leaking
    OS-level details. TEA wrote tests but they may be narrow. Partial catch via TEA.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer''s data flow trace explicitly states: ''The tenant ID is a raw
    String throughout, not the TenantId newtype from axiathon-core. This bypasses
    validation.'' Also flagged silent header skip as blocking issue #3. TEA also wrote
    header injection tests covering CRLF in tenant ID.'
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding [MEDIUM]: ''clap_complete, comfy-table, dirs, csv, keyring,
    reqwest, and toml are declared directly in the crate''s Cargo.toml instead of
    being declared in [workspace.dependencies]... This violates the workspace dependency
    management pattern.'''
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding [HIGH]: ''ClientConfig derives Deserialize without #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)].
    A typo like servr_url or a config key from a future version will be silently ignored.''
    Listed as strongly recommended fix #4.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...). The reviewer flagged other vacuous tests (no_color, header injection)
    but not this specific one in config tests.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic with
    'let _ = config'. TEA wrote 13 config tests but did not identify this specific
    test as having no meaningful assertions.
